--- a/doc/README.build.msvc.html
+++ b/doc/README.build.msvc.html
@@ -109,6 +109,7 @@ with the default options (next, next, next)</li>
 <li>make_all.bat [DEBUG] [CLEAN]</li>
 </ol>
 <li>To skip the Cloop build and generated interface updates, pass <code>WITHOUT_CLOOP_GENERATION</code> to <code>run_all.bat</code>.</li>
+<li>To use boost headers from the system include path (e.g. the <code>INCLUDE</code> environment variable) instead of <code>extern\boost</code>, pass <code>WITH_SYSTEM_BOOST</code> to <code>make_boot.bat</code> (or <code>run_all.bat</code>). The choice is recorded in <code>temp\&lt;Platform&gt;\FirebirdSystemBoost.props</code> and used by later builds, including from the IDE; a <code>make_boot.bat</code> run without the option removes it, and so does <code>clean_all.bat</code>. The installed <code>Message.h</code> then uses <code>&lt;boost/...&gt;</code> and the embedded boost copy is not distributed.</li>
 </ol>
 <ul>
 <p>After the build finish, an output directory with the binaries is created below your firebird directory.</p>
